## Mixed files

Three places in the tree mix the two licences. In every case the rule is the
same: **the licence follows the substance, not the file extension.**

1. **In-game text inside code.** The player-facing strings assembled into the
   frontend and HUD live in `src/main.s` (for example `main.s:6921` and
   `:7309-7344`: `START GAME`, `OPTIONS`, `TOP SCORES`, `SCORE`, `HULL`). The
   file is MIT; those literal strings are in-game text and remain under
   CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Reusing the *code* needs nothing from this file; shipping
   the *words* does.
2. **Asset data quoted inside code and tests.** Converters under `scripts/` and
   expectations under `tests/` embed fragments of asset data (glyph rows,
   palettes, hull maps) to validate the conversion. The surrounding code is MIT;
   the embedded asset fragments remain under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
3. **The released binaries.** `dist/void-strike-65.xex`,
   `dist/void-strike-65.atr` and the release `.zip` are a **combined work**: MIT
   code linked together with CC BY-NC-SA assets. Distribute them under the more
   restrictive of the two — that is, **non-commercially, with attribution and
   under the same terms**. They are free to share, play and pass on to other
   Atari users on that basis.

## Third-party

**Nothing third-party is vendored in this repository.** All code, art, music and
text here is original work by the copyright holder.

Two external components are used but not included:

- **Atari800** (GPL-2.0) — the emulator used for automated runtime measurement
  and boot smoke. `scripts/atari800-wall-trace.h`,
  `scripts/atari800-capacity-watch.h` and `scripts/measure-frame-profile.h` are
  **our own code**, MIT-licensed, compiled *into* a locally fetched Atari800
  source tree under `build/` (untracked). MIT is compatible with GPL-2.0: a
  binary built from that combination is covered by the GPL, and no Atari800
  source is redistributed here.
- **cc65 / ca65** and the `romdev-toolchain-cc65` npm package — the assembler and
  C toolchain, installed at build time under `node_modules/` (untracked) and
  distributed under their own licences.

The Atari 8-bit computer character set is referenced from the machine's own OS
ROM at runtime; no ROM bytes are contained in this repository. This project is a
non-commercial hobby work, not affiliated with or endorsed by Atari.
